# ─── Append these lines to your project's existing .gitignore ───
# Prevents session artifacts, signing keys, and local config from leaking into the repo.

# Session and planning artifacts (never commit these)
# Ignore all hidden files and folders (dotfiles/dotdirs) not explicitly tracked
.*
# ... but a blanket .* also swallows the repo plumbing, including .gitignore ITSELF, which means the
# ignore rules never reach a fresh clone, and .github, which means CI workflows can never be
# committed. Re-include the files that are genuinely part of the project. Found 2026-07-22.
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.editorconfig
!.github/
# Local tooling docs and working notes (suffix convention)
*.dev
openspec/
plan.md
scratch.md
notes.md
*.session
*.tmp
.env
.env*
*.env

# Keystores and signing keys (NEVER commit)
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
key.properties
keystore.properties
android/key.properties

# Local override files
local.properties
android/local.properties
*.local

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Build outputs
build/
dist/

# Python artifacts (Python/GTK4 and other Python projects)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Operator-specific: analysis doc + real per-install profiles stay local (not published).
# Ignore every profile except the published example (do not name a real box here).
docs/MANIFEST.md
profiles/*.toml
!profiles/example.toml

# Internal-only, not part of the public open-core surface (kept locally, never published)
AGENTS.md
PROJECT.md
TASKS.md
docs/PLAN.md
docs/THREAT-MODEL.md
docs/secret-rotation-comparison.md
docs/DECISION-one-engine.md
docs/DECISION-agent-workspace-primitives.md
docs/DECISION-agent-trust-latency.md
